"""Provisional v2 train-only build, local and unpublished (L7b values: T1 decoded and re-fitted on outer-train rows).

DEFAULT (--split-version registry-epoch0, unchanged): per epoch-0 context (scale_check.resolve_context lineage), the
outer-train/test rows R/T are the epoch-0 context's (the registry folds, jope.virtual-splits/v1 grouped-stratified-
kfold/v1). Writes under OUT/<shard>/<view_id>/:
  encoder.jtt1.gz   train-only min-max JTT1 (t1prep.prepare): the encoders' training-side input
  teacher.jtt1.gz   same rows, columns and inner folds, values re-fitted (categories re-coded, target copies dropped)
                    but NOT min-max scaled: the evaluator in patch 0001 scales per fit on its own fit rows
  a0.f32            A0 meta-features of encoder.jtt1 (metafeatures.from_raw)
  context.json      identities, sha256 of every file, t1prep strata, code sha256, values mode, published=false
  .done             written last; a context with .done is skipped (resumable, idempotent)
Per shard: shard-<i>-of-<n>.receipt.json (expected vs done vs failed). No S3, network or GPU; nothing is published.

SPLIT V2 (--split-version rowsel-raw-split-v2; owner ruling NONRAW-SPLIT-A, owner-decisions-20261006T053215Z.json). The
registry split reads y through its exact full-row duplicate key (receipts/trainonly-v2/split-scope-nonraw-20261006T034028Z
.json), so the non-raw contexts are re-split with the raw route's target-free split v2 (dltrain/rowsel_raw_split_v2.py,
used unmodified):
  scope       plan.json from a pinned publish manifest (clean-v1 L7b datasets, or the research clean datasets); a dataset
              is in scope with ALL its epoch-0 contexts (replacement is per dataset)
  universe    every row of the dataset's epoch-0 data object A as this tool reads it (scale_check.resolve_context: the T1
              table). Epoch-0 coverage, checked per dataset: every epoch-0 context's R u T is all of A (R = complement of
              the registry test fold), and A is the whole T1 table (manifest sample_rows == source_rows for every
              in-scope dataset). So the epoch-0 clean views covered the whole T1 table, in 1-5 registry folds.
              Position = 0-based row index in A.
  partition   "t1" (the universe label in the row rank; tools/v2_build_l7a.py uses "l7a" for its matched source rows)
  groups      exact parsed float64 bytes of the T1 FEATURE columns (categorical columns as their T1-coded value, a
              bijection of the code); the target column is never part of the key
  folds       rowsel_raw_split_v2.outer_split(h, positions, values, specs, partition="t1"): 5 folds, all built
  per fold    T = fold f, R = every other position (both ascending), then exactly the default build: t1prep refit on R,
              train-only min-max, inner 2-fold labels from R, target-copy drop on R, JTT1 train rows then test rows
  gates       split: no duplicate group straddles folds, the target permuted/replaced/constant never moves it
              (rowsel_raw.split_target_check), and duplicate-preserving outer-test feature/target changes of every fold
              never move it (rowsel_raw_split_v2.value_check); per context: the train side (scaler, encoder and teacher
              train rows, inner labels, A0, train-side refit report) is bit-identical when the outer-test rows are
              perturbed, and the gate's own base equals the written artifacts; the new view_id collides with no
              existing view_id (holdout denylist v2 and every context.json under build-v2, frozen at plan time)
  identity    top-level `cut` {cut_id "trainonly-split-v2:" + split sha256 exactly as rowsel_raw_split_v2 returns it,
              schema, partition, replaces_cut (the registry split object sha256), comparable_with_replaced false};
              `split` (the raw route's split record fields); view_id <h>__r0__f<f>__l7bsplit2_<identity[:12]>;
              `epoch0_replaced` (dataset level)
  writes      only when all 5 folds pass every gate: files + context.json of every fold, then .done of every fold.
              A .done context is never rewritten; its recorded identity and files must equal the recomputed ones.
              The tree gets plan.json, existing-view-ids.json, _datasets/<h>.json per dataset and, after the verified
              summary, .complete (all create-only).

Usage (inside the lane slice, RUN/tmp/p2fix3/py.sh):
  v2_build_local.py --out DIR --shard I --of N [--views v1,v2]                     registry folds (unchanged default)
  v2_build_local.py --split-version rowsel-raw-split-v2 --plan {clean-l7b,research-clean} --out NEW_TREE --of N
  v2_build_local.py --split-version rowsel-raw-split-v2 --out NEW_TREE --shard I --of N [--datasets h1,h2]
  v2_build_local.py --split-version rowsel-raw-split-v2 --summarize --out NEW_TREE --of N --tests-log LOG --mutants JSON
                    [--pilot JSON] [--receipt-stem STEM]
